# ── The slot map ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   name | port | card | weights folder | arguments
#
#   card    a driver index (0, 1, …), `all` for a model split across every
#           card, or `cpu` for a model that never touches a GPU
#   weights an absolute path, or a folder name relative to ~/models
#
# ONE CONTAINER PER SLOT, including when two slots serve the SAME weights
# file on two different cards. A container freezes its command line when it
# is created, so a slot that shared a container would need recreating on
# every swap — which is exactly the kind of hidden step that makes a map
# drift away from the machine.
#
# The names below are illustrative. Replace them with your own; the
# turnstile reads this file on every request, so there is nothing to restart
# after an edit.
#
# ── The grid this describes ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   footprint   card 1 alone | card 0 alone | both together
#   preset      standard | coder | generalist | fast | long | big
#
# A preset name means the same thing on every footprint. The release slots
# (free-c0, free-c1, free-all) are NOT listed here: they load nothing, and
# the service derives them from the cards it discovers.

# ── card 1: the assistant that is always there ──────────────────────────
assistant-c1|8095|1|my-9b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8095 -m /models/my-9b-Q8_0.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99
coder-c1|8100|1|my-14b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8100 -m /models/my-14b-Q6_K.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99
generalist-c1|8101|1|my-12b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8101 -m /models/my-12b-Q6_K.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99

# ── card 0: the card you allocate ───────────────────────────────────────
coder-c0|8110|0|my-14b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8110 -m /models/my-14b-Q6_K.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99
generalist-c0|8111|0|my-12b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8111 -m /models/my-12b-Q6_K.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99

# ── both cards: what does not fit on one ────────────────────────────────
big-x2|8120|all|my-27b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8120 -m /models/my-27b-IQ4_XS.gguf -c 26624 -ngl 99 -ts 1,1
long-x2|8121|all|my-9b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8121 -m /models/my-9b-Q8_0.gguf -c 131072 -ngl 99 -ts 1,1

# ── CPU: never stopped, answers during every swap ───────────────────────
#
# This is the one that keeps the machine usable while a card is loading.
# The swap logic skips `cpu` slots explicitly — an earlier version did not,
# and killed them.
fallback|8084|cpu|my-3b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8084 -m /models/my-3b-Q6_K.gguf -c 8192
completion|8085|cpu|my-1.5b|--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8085 -m /models/my-1.5b-Q6_K.gguf -c 8192
